## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply progressive hydration, per-column lazy-loading, and worker offloading to meet Lighthouse budgets in a heavy dashboard. Also probes SSR/CSR trade-offs and how to validate improvements.

## Key Concepts

- Progressive hydration
- Dynamic imports and code-splitting
- Virtualization
- Web Workers
- Lighthouse budgets and metrics
- IntersectionObserver for loading offscreen content

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example skeleton: dynamic import of heavy cell renderer
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic';
const HeavyCell = dynamic(() => import('./cells/HeavyCell'));

// Progressive hydration with IntersectionObserver
const useColumnHydration = (columnRef) => {
  const [isHydrated, setIsHydrated] = useState(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      ([entry]) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          setIsHydrated(true);
          observer.disconnect();
        }
      },
      { threshold: 0.1 }
    );

    if (columnRef.current) {
      observer.observe(columnRef.current);
    }

    return () => observer.disconnect();
  }, []);

  return isHydrated;
};
```

